    "suggested_action": "replace_ja_expression",
    "reason": "The English lemma 'spell' (noun) in a magic context typically refers to an incantation or a magical effect. The Japanese expression '魔力' (maryoku) primarily means 'magical power' or 'supernatural power,' which is the ability or energy to perform magic, not the incantation or effect itself. While related, they are distinct concepts for a learner. The most natural Japanese equivalents for 'spell' (incantation/charm) would be 魔法 (mahō) or 呪文 (jumon).",
